=== task: order easy
title: One pass, step by step
prompt: Put the steps of one pass of selection sort in order.
items:
- Take the item at `start` as the smallest so far: `smallest = start`
- Scan the items after it, moving `smallest` to any item that's smaller
- Swap the item at `start` with the item at `smallest`
- Move `start` one place right, for the next pass
hint: The scan needs a smallest-so-far to compare with.
hint: The swap can only happen once the scan has looked at every unsorted item.
right: Start with the first unsorted item, scan the rest, swap once, then move on to the next place.
wrong: A pass starts with `smallest = start`, scans the rest of the list, and swaps only after the scan. Then `start` moves on.

