fail[2]: A sorted list needs no real swaps.
fail[3]: Each pass moves the 1, then the 2, then the 3 into place, and each swap leaves the next one out of place: 3.
fail[5]: Pass 1 swaps the first 2 with a 1, and pass 2 swaps the other 2 with the other 1: 2.
fail[6]: The list should end up sorted, [1, 2, 3], after 2 swaps.
